<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Broad Front (Uruguay)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1971">1971</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Frente Amplio</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Broad Front, or Frente Amplio, is a left-wing coalition of parties in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruguay">Uruguay</a> founded in 1971. Banned under the military dictatorship of 1973–1985, it governed from 2005 to 2020 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabare-vazquez">Tabaré Vázquez</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-mujica">José Mujica</a> and returned to office in 2025 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamandu-orsi">Yamandú Orsi</a>. Its governments expanded social programmes and legalised same-sex marriage and cannabis.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/broad-front-uruguay.jpg" alt="Broad Front (Uruguay)" width="320" height="223" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Frente Amplio · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Frente_Amplio_2025_logo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
